From ffd3885e66b0f65bd123ecd46c4154543149b3de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 04:00:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] config: add selectable restricted UCI profiles

Some systems must start netifd with only a small, explicitly chosen
part of the network configuration. Loading everything and then removing
interfaces can expose links which should remain isolated.

Allow UCI sections to carry a profile option. When a profile is
selected, load only matching sections while retaining loopback and
global settings. Suppress procd and ucode configuration sources because
they cannot carry the UCI profile marker.

Before each configuration load, synchronously run executable selectors
from the config-selectors.d addon directory. Empty output abstains. A
valid profile name selects a restricted view. Reject selector failures,
invalid output and conflicting selections before changing active network
state.

This lets packages choose a fail-closed network view without changing
netifd service lifecycle or delaying process startup.

Signed-off-by: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
---
 CMakeLists.txt    |   2 +-
 config-selector.c | 237 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 config-selector.h |  15 +++
 config.c          |  78 +++++++++++++--
 main.c            |   1 +
 netifd.h          |   1 +
 6 files changed, 325 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 config-selector.c
 create mode 100644 config-selector.h

